1
00:00:00,176 --> 00:00:01,576
[Previously]
Why are you doing this?

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,401
What you and Tokyo
are doing really isn't safe.

3
00:00:04,496 --> 00:00:07,160
Tokyo could end up in danger too.

4
00:00:07,488 --> 00:00:11,341
We can handle our own relationships.
We don't need you interfering.

5
00:00:12,766 --> 00:00:15,840
We're not going to break
up because of anyone else.

6
00:00:16,078 --> 00:00:17,479
If we ever do break up,

7
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:19,880
it should be because we
don't love each other anymore.

8
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:50,387
You can go now. The party is over.

9
00:00:50,552 --> 00:00:52,152
And people will start to come back here.

10
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:54,054
Okay.

11
00:00:56,238 --> 00:00:57,450
I'm sweaty.

12
00:01:00,616 --> 00:01:01,617
Come on.

13
00:01:03,958 --> 00:01:04,959
You should go.

14
00:01:07,019 --> 00:01:08,620
Wait…just a minute.

15
00:01:13,987 --> 00:01:15,200
What are you doing?

16
00:01:17,544 --> 00:01:18,880
Tokyo!

17
00:01:19,652 --> 00:01:21,320
The teachers planted these roses.

18
00:01:24,611 --> 00:01:26,920
It's okay, just one rose.

19
00:01:29,059 --> 00:01:30,460
What are you doing?

20
00:01:31,387 --> 00:01:32,600
Gosh, you're bleeding.

21
00:01:33,326 --> 00:01:34,427
It's okay.

22
00:01:37,912 --> 00:01:38,913
Here, this is for you.

23
00:01:47,246 --> 00:01:48,247
Are you hitting on me?

24
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:51,641
Not really.

25
00:01:56,041 --> 00:01:57,242
I won you over ages ago.

26
00:02:05,739 --> 00:02:06,920
You can go now.

27
00:02:07,078 --> 00:02:08,720
Yeah, I know.

28
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:10,320
I'm really leaving now.

29
00:02:11,686 --> 00:02:12,687
Bye.

30
00:02:31,464 --> 00:02:32,465
Tokyo.

31
00:02:36,275 --> 00:02:37,276
Can I talk to you?

32
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:52,400
"Juliet &amp; Juliet" (Episode 5)

33
00:02:59,942 --> 00:03:02,680
Well? Are you ready to tell me?

34
00:03:05,446 --> 00:03:06,840
I told you, it's nothing.

35
00:03:08,166 --> 00:03:09,450
Why can't you just believe me?

36
00:03:09,750 --> 00:03:11,070
How am I supposed to believe you?

37
00:03:17,158 --> 00:03:19,100
How could you do this?

38
00:03:22,679 --> 00:03:25,400
You're lying to Dad and to me.

39
00:03:25,710 --> 00:03:26,800
You're lying to Big.

40
00:03:26,926 --> 00:03:28,526
You're lying to everyone in this family.

41
00:03:29,902 --> 00:03:31,440
You're betraying the Kongpurim family.

42
00:03:33,262 --> 00:03:34,462
It's because of her, isn't it?

43
00:03:34,923 --> 00:03:37,843
Is that why you want to study in England?
What the hell are you thinking?

44
00:03:45,050 --> 00:03:47,080
This has nothing to do with Blue, Yi.

45
00:03:50,971 --> 00:03:52,672
I just don't want to stay here.

46
00:03:55,131 --> 00:03:57,132
Because you and Dad are always like this.

47
00:04:01,926 --> 00:04:04,640
The girl from that family has
completely brainwashed you, Tokyo.

48
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:09,500
Don't you ever stop and think, Yi?

49
00:04:10,931 --> 00:04:13,000
All you do is obsess over
which side everyone is on

50
00:04:13,422 --> 00:04:14,700
and who's going to strike first.

51
00:04:14,723 --> 00:04:15,724
Tokyo!

52
00:04:29,792 --> 00:04:32,312
Do you really want to live like this
for the rest of your life?

53
00:04:37,955 --> 00:04:40,600
If you want to stay here, then stay.

54
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:47,440
But my dreams aren't here.

55
00:04:51,001 --> 00:04:52,920
I want to go out and see the world.

56
00:04:53,267 --> 00:04:55,100
I don't want to stay here.

57
00:04:55,358 --> 00:04:56,359
No.

58
00:04:57,624 --> 00:04:58,680
No means no.

59
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:01,920
No matter what, you're
better off staying home.

60
00:05:04,682 --> 00:05:05,986
How would that be better for me?

61
00:05:08,123 --> 00:05:10,243
Have you ever tried leaving
and doing something else?

62
00:05:11,220 --> 00:05:13,770
Have you ever tried stepping out
from under Dad's shadow?

63
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,520
You've never even tried.

64
00:05:17,856 --> 00:05:19,960
So how would you know which life is better?

65
00:05:22,091 --> 00:05:24,920
Won't you let me try
living my own life for once?

66
00:05:26,726 --> 00:05:28,600
Stop making excuses.

67
00:05:29,264 --> 00:05:30,565
Do you think I don't know

68
00:05:30,784 --> 00:05:32,920
you only want to follow
that girl from that family?

69
00:05:39,200 --> 00:05:41,201
Tokyo, if you don't stop,

70
00:05:42,287 --> 00:05:43,406
I'll show you

71
00:05:43,784 --> 00:05:45,885
what the eldest son of the Kongpurim family

72
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:47,680
is capable of putting an end to.

73
00:06:00,033 --> 00:06:01,353
Come on. Put some effort into it.

74
00:06:05,744 --> 00:06:07,200
You're so useless.

75
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:09,632
Who the hell would be afraid of you?

76
00:06:19,470 --> 00:06:20,491
Has Big told you yet

77
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:23,320
when we can reopen our casino?

78
00:06:24,790 --> 00:06:25,791
Not yet, Dad.

79
00:06:26,710 --> 00:06:28,590
But if we keep running
short of cash like this,

80
00:06:28,966 --> 00:06:30,467
all our men will desert us.

81
00:06:32,550 --> 00:06:35,091
Especially if we have to go up against
the Monchaitrakul family right now.

82
00:06:35,115 --> 00:06:36,320
I'm not even sure

83
00:06:37,552 --> 00:06:38,553
we can handle them.

84
00:06:39,691 --> 00:06:41,400
Commander Sin just warned us

85
00:06:42,648 --> 00:06:44,040
about going after them.

86
00:06:45,032 --> 00:06:48,160
That's why I don't want to risk
a direct confrontation right now.

87
00:06:55,220 --> 00:06:58,021
So, what's going on
between Tokyo and that girl?

88
00:07:01,574 --> 00:07:02,575
Well...

89
00:07:06,358 --> 00:07:09,100
Nothing has happened yet, Dad.

90
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,400
Don't let me find out later

91
00:07:14,475 --> 00:07:15,476
that you chickened out.

92
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:20,401
Yes, sir.

93
00:07:58,331 --> 00:07:59,840
Did you tell Pakkad?

94
00:08:08,112 --> 00:08:09,113
And…

95
00:08:11,930 --> 00:08:13,451
Who do you think sent the photo?

96
00:08:17,334 --> 00:08:18,335
I don't know.

97
00:08:20,731 --> 00:08:21,732
It could be...

98
00:08:22,694 --> 00:08:24,520
anyone.

99
00:08:25,872 --> 00:08:27,300
Anyone at this school.

100
00:08:29,232 --> 00:08:31,120
Then we can't trust anyone at all.

101
00:08:33,637 --> 00:08:34,638
Yeah.

102
00:08:39,454 --> 00:08:40,455
What are you doing?

103
00:08:41,854 --> 00:08:43,214
Applying through direct admission.

104
00:08:44,590 --> 00:08:46,670
I'm thinking of going to
the same university as you.

105
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:48,721
What?

106
00:08:48,821 --> 00:08:49,822
Yeah.

107
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:52,140
Let's go to Bangkok and
take the entrance exam together.

108
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:53,370
Then we can study together.

109
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:55,781
Which faculty are you applying to?

110
00:08:58,843 --> 00:08:59,844
Um...

111
00:09:01,220 --> 00:09:02,260
Maybe the Faculty of Arts.

112
00:09:04,699 --> 00:09:06,600
Honestly, I'm still not entirely sure.

113
00:09:07,696 --> 00:09:08,697
But

114
00:09:10,414 --> 00:09:12,240
if I don't do something now,

115
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:16,040
I'll be stuck here for the rest of my life.

116
00:09:24,873 --> 00:09:27,280
[University application to the faculty of
law, with a middling chance of getting in]

117
00:09:28,339 --> 00:09:30,039
[English linguistics, a
good chance of getting in]

118
00:09:31,904 --> 00:09:33,344
Then let's apply to this university.

119
00:09:34,498 --> 00:09:36,766
Last year's cutoff score wasn't very high.

120
00:09:36,790 --> 00:09:38,470
We might both have a chance of getting in.

121
00:09:39,867 --> 00:09:40,868
No.

122
00:09:41,446 --> 00:09:43,480
That's not the university
you want to attend.

123
00:09:44,363 --> 00:09:45,520
It's okay.

124
00:09:47,302 --> 00:09:48,303
No, it's not.

125
00:09:48,939 --> 00:09:51,416
Look. The exam's on the same day
as the one for Srisilapasat University

126
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:52,480
that you want to get into.

127
00:09:53,912 --> 00:09:55,520
It's fine. Let's go with this one.

128
00:09:57,075 --> 00:09:58,076
Okay?

129
00:09:58,136 --> 00:10:01,000
Then in two weeks, we'll go to Bangkok
and take the exam together.

130
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:18,827
All right, class.

131
00:10:19,782 --> 00:10:21,650
Open your books to page 75.

132
00:10:22,230 --> 00:10:25,600
We're still studying European history.

133
00:10:57,800 --> 00:10:59,301
This wasn't you, was it?

134
00:11:01,296 --> 00:11:02,400
Of course not.

135
00:11:02,497 --> 00:11:05,337
What kind of person do you think I
am? I'm your cousin, for God's sake.

136
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:07,560
Damn it.

137
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:13,360
How the hell did this go from a
cute romance to a freaking thriller?

138
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:15,080
Then who do you think did it?

139
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:18,920
I don't know. That's why I'm freaking out.

140
00:11:24,450 --> 00:11:25,451
Unless...

141
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:28,441
it was Tokyo's friends.

142
00:11:30,187 --> 00:11:31,688
It's possible.

143
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:34,560
Remember when you first transferred here?

144
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:36,321
Remember what I told you?

145
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:40,257
That Pupae and Jai only became friends with
Tokyo because they were scared of her dad.

146
00:11:40,281 --> 00:11:41,482
I'm serious. It's true.

147
00:11:59,032 --> 00:12:00,600
- What?
- Hey!

148
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:03,520
- What the hell?
- Get someone to help. Hurry!

149
00:12:03,541 --> 00:12:05,242
- Let's go!
- Okay.

150
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:14,681
[Everything's going according to plan.]

151
00:12:35,227 --> 00:12:36,960
Sorry to bother you, Wiboon.

152
00:12:37,179 --> 00:12:39,000
About the accident at the pier,

153
00:12:39,275 --> 00:12:42,130
I'm afraid we'll have to suspend
all construction work by your company

154
00:12:42,902 --> 00:12:45,960
until we've investigated the accident
and established what happened.

155
00:12:48,528 --> 00:12:49,529
I understand.

156
00:12:50,299 --> 00:12:52,500
And I'm willing to fully cooperate.

157
00:13:02,995 --> 00:13:06,579
I just hope everything
gets resolved in time

158
00:13:07,536 --> 00:13:09,336
for me to hand over
the project as scheduled.

159
00:13:11,054 --> 00:13:12,080
I'd like to help,

160
00:13:12,675 --> 00:13:15,475
but this time, you'll have to
follow the proper procedure, Mr. Wiboon.

161
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:18,561
Excuse me.

162
00:13:28,811 --> 00:13:31,120
Miss Tokyo, I'll pick you up after school.

163
00:13:56,203 --> 00:13:57,204
Hey,

164
00:13:58,347 --> 00:13:59,348
what is going on?

165
00:14:01,414 --> 00:14:04,160
It was May's dad. The
scaffolding collapsed on him.

166
00:14:04,336 --> 00:14:06,137
So people are pissed.

167
00:14:06,237 --> 00:14:09,200
They think the Monchaitrakul family
took over and started cutting corners.

168
00:14:09,302 --> 00:14:11,702
Things weren't like this
when the Kongpurims were in charge.

169
00:14:22,102 --> 00:14:24,403
Hey, aren't you gonna turn in your phone?

170
00:14:24,528 --> 00:14:26,429
You just got it. Paew's
gonna confiscate it.

171
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:10,301
Aren't you coming?

172
00:15:15,104 --> 00:15:16,360
What are you gonna do?

173
00:15:23,576 --> 00:15:24,577
I'm sure...

174
00:15:26,771 --> 00:15:28,040
Pae and Jai

175
00:15:28,686 --> 00:15:30,640
weren't the ones who sold our photo to Yi.

176
00:15:32,880 --> 00:15:33,881
But...

177
00:15:35,256 --> 00:15:36,496
something's still bothering me.

178
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:00,960
That photo Yi got

179
00:16:01,726 --> 00:16:03,486
was so blurry you could
barely see anything.

180
00:16:05,459 --> 00:16:07,019
There's no way it came from this phone.

181
00:16:07,554 --> 00:16:08,560
So we can stop worrying.

182
00:16:09,955 --> 00:16:10,956
Yeah, I guess.

183
00:16:11,704 --> 00:16:14,130
But how did Pae suddenly get a new phone?

184
00:16:15,507 --> 00:16:17,720
Her family's already
up to their necks in debt.

185
00:16:26,299 --> 00:16:27,960
Why don't you just ask her?

186
00:16:29,264 --> 00:16:30,961
I asked Pakkad straight up.

187
00:16:35,475 --> 00:16:39,000
Hey! Why are you going through our lockers?

188
00:16:46,179 --> 00:16:47,760
I just needed to borrow a pad.

189
00:16:48,880 --> 00:16:49,881
I forgot to bring one.

190
00:16:59,672 --> 00:17:00,673
Go ahead.

191
00:17:04,235 --> 00:17:05,236
Thanks.

192
00:17:25,100 --> 00:17:27,451
Dad, are you really going through
with opening another casino?

193
00:17:27,475 --> 00:17:28,800
You thought I was kidding?

194
00:17:29,550 --> 00:17:30,801
I'm on my way to Korat

195
00:17:31,699 --> 00:17:33,140
to raise some money for it.

196
00:17:34,483 --> 00:17:36,443
But I am about to become
a police inspector, Dad.

197
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:37,840
Can't you wait a little longer?

198
00:17:39,697 --> 00:17:41,998
If I wait for you, we'll be broke by then.

199
00:17:42,446 --> 00:17:44,840
Didn't I tell you to wrap
up that case at the pier?

200
00:17:45,304 --> 00:17:47,550
The Monchaitrakuls finally screwed up.

201
00:17:48,339 --> 00:17:49,840
I wanna bury them for good.

202
00:17:51,224 --> 00:17:52,225
I know, Dad.

203
00:17:52,632 --> 00:17:53,880
Just give me some time.

204
00:17:55,053 --> 00:17:58,120
Finding enough evidence to get
their concession revoked isn't that easy.

205
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:02,200
A fish that never bites

206
00:18:02,921 --> 00:18:04,440
may look harmless.

207
00:18:05,356 --> 00:18:06,600
But in my eyes,

208
00:18:07,955 --> 00:18:09,880
it's nothing but weak prey.

209
00:18:23,955 --> 00:18:24,956
Dad?

210
00:18:46,126 --> 00:18:47,512
Evening, Boss.

211
00:18:47,700 --> 00:18:48,701
Hey.

212
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,730
So, how's your daughter
liking her new phone?

213
00:18:56,467 --> 00:18:59,168
She loves it. Can't put the thing down.

214
00:19:01,627 --> 00:19:03,200
Thanks again, Boss.

215
00:19:03,622 --> 00:19:05,880
Pupae had been using
that old phone forever.

216
00:19:07,350 --> 00:19:10,000
I just couldn't afford
to get her a new one.

217
00:19:10,907 --> 00:19:11,908
Don't mention it.

218
00:19:12,272 --> 00:19:13,700
I've known her since she was a kid.

219
00:19:13,931 --> 00:19:15,880
She's practically family.

220
00:19:17,896 --> 00:19:19,627
About that thing you
asked me to take care of...

221
00:19:19,651 --> 00:19:20,720
It's done.

222
00:19:21,678 --> 00:19:25,200
I've got almost all the local
transport operators on board.

223
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:26,801
Good.

224
00:19:27,494 --> 00:19:30,250
The pier closes tomorrow
for the accident investigation.

225
00:19:30,518 --> 00:19:32,880
That'll make things
tough for the local vendors.

226
00:19:33,100 --> 00:19:35,158
The locals need to remember

227
00:19:35,211 --> 00:19:37,560
who they turn to when times get tough.

228
00:19:40,440 --> 00:19:41,600
If there's nothing else,

229
00:19:41,984 --> 00:19:43,320
I'll be going, Boss.

230
00:19:43,480 --> 00:19:44,520
- Oh, bye.
- Bye, sir.

231
00:19:44,581 --> 00:19:45,920
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

232
00:19:49,840 --> 00:19:51,960
If there's anything you
need, just let me know.

233
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:54,170
I'll take care of everything.

234
00:19:54,558 --> 00:19:56,160
There's only one thing I want.

235
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:58,620
I need the pier reopened
as soon as possible.

236
00:19:59,784 --> 00:20:01,550
If you don't mind me saying Wiboon,

237
00:20:02,067 --> 00:20:04,267
I think you should stop
trying to pull strings for now.

238
00:20:04,440 --> 00:20:06,120
You've already stepped down. Just lay low.

239
00:20:06,408 --> 00:20:08,680
No one wants to get dragged into this mess.

240
00:20:13,054 --> 00:20:14,455
The workers are awake, Boss.

241
00:20:15,055 --> 00:20:17,215
They confirmed they set up
the scaffolding themselves.

242
00:20:17,422 --> 00:20:19,342
There's no way it could've
collapsed on its own.

243
00:20:19,606 --> 00:20:20,960
But as they were leaving,

244
00:20:21,310 --> 00:20:23,320
they saw two new workers come in.

245
00:20:24,184 --> 00:20:26,360
We're looking into who they were.

246
00:20:28,344 --> 00:20:30,345
Make sure we cover all their expenses.

247
00:20:30,799 --> 00:20:32,800
And keep them safe as our witnesses.

248
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:34,001
Yes, Boss.

249
00:21:03,280 --> 00:21:06,040
I asked her to help Phu
with the insurance paperwork.

250
00:21:06,281 --> 00:21:08,200
She gets a little extra for helping out.

251
00:21:09,500 --> 00:21:10,960
Go with Phu to the other room.

252
00:21:21,501 --> 00:21:22,502
Want some water?

253
00:21:42,432 --> 00:21:45,445
We made the right call
moving here, didn't we?

254
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:51,320
We could always move back
to build housing developments.

255
00:21:53,800 --> 00:21:54,801
No.

256
00:21:56,256 --> 00:21:58,200
This is where we belong.

257
00:22:00,048 --> 00:22:01,200
We were here before them.

258
00:22:14,486 --> 00:22:16,566
So you're really gonna take
the entrance exam there?

259
00:22:17,278 --> 00:22:18,438
You sure you won't regret it?

260
00:22:22,051 --> 00:22:23,152
Of course I will.

261
00:22:24,318 --> 00:22:25,480
But what else can I do?

262
00:22:30,262 --> 00:22:31,263
I don't know.

263
00:22:32,598 --> 00:22:34,680
I don't even know where
things are going with us.

264
00:22:35,890 --> 00:22:37,090
It's such a freaking headache.

265
00:22:37,571 --> 00:22:38,760
Whoa, you've got it bad.

266
00:22:39,230 --> 00:22:41,200
You're really giving up
your dream for one girl?

267
00:22:43,427 --> 00:22:45,680
What if you and Tokyo break up before then?

268
00:22:47,352 --> 00:22:49,450
What if one of you gives up first?

269
00:23:27,374 --> 00:23:29,814
In two weeks, we'll go to Bangkok
and take the exam together.

270
00:23:30,240 --> 00:23:31,641
Why the long face?

271
00:23:32,834 --> 00:23:35,113
Because you're giving up your dream for me.

272
00:23:40,720 --> 00:23:41,880
Don't overthink it.

273
00:23:43,462 --> 00:23:45,856
You're giving up your family,

274
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:47,440
your home, everything here.

275
00:23:49,856 --> 00:23:51,560
So we're meeting each other halfway.

276
00:23:52,928 --> 00:23:55,120
I give up a little, you give up a little,

277
00:24:00,907 --> 00:24:02,250
so we can be together.

278
00:24:06,300 --> 00:24:07,301
You mean it?

279
00:24:21,960 --> 00:24:25,640
[Bangkok Entrance Exam Meet
at the bus station, 5:00 AM]

280
00:25:29,579 --> 00:25:31,100
Bangkok! Hop on!

281
00:25:31,515 --> 00:25:34,680
Bangkok! Get on! We're
leaving as soon as we're full!

282
00:25:34,704 --> 00:25:36,664
[Blue: Where are you?
The bus is about to leave.]

283
00:25:49,294 --> 00:25:50,574
Where do you think you're going?

284
00:25:52,640 --> 00:25:53,641
To take an exam.

285
00:25:53,960 --> 00:25:54,961
Where?

286
00:25:56,264 --> 00:25:57,265
Bangkok.

287
00:25:58,302 --> 00:25:59,662
You're going with her, aren't you?

288
00:26:01,635 --> 00:26:02,636
Come here.

289
00:26:03,560 --> 00:26:05,400
No! Let go of me.

290
00:26:06,686 --> 00:26:07,720
You're so mean!

291
00:26:08,959 --> 00:26:10,519
Why do you have to be so damn stubborn?

292
00:26:11,332 --> 00:26:13,932
You love her so much you're
willing to leave your family for her?

293
00:26:14,800 --> 00:26:15,801
I love her.

294
00:26:17,700 --> 00:26:19,720
But I love Dad and you guys too.

295
00:26:20,552 --> 00:26:22,553
If you love us, then choose us.

296
00:26:22,600 --> 00:26:23,960
Why would you choose her?

297
00:26:31,944 --> 00:26:34,320
I've chosen you and Dad my whole life.

298
00:26:35,614 --> 00:26:37,560
Can I choose myself for once?

299
00:26:38,179 --> 00:26:40,440
If I don't, I know I'll regret it forever.

300
00:26:42,083 --> 00:26:44,200
I just wanna go out and live my own life.

301
00:26:45,236 --> 00:26:47,100
I wanna make my own choices for once.

302
00:26:48,846 --> 00:26:50,000
And if I fail...

303
00:26:51,352 --> 00:26:53,272
can't it at least be
because of a choice I made?

304
00:27:01,803 --> 00:27:03,936
Hey, are you getting on or not?

305
00:27:04,700 --> 00:27:05,880
We're about to leave.

306
00:27:08,144 --> 00:27:09,260
I'm coming.

307
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:10,401
Blue.

308
00:27:11,765 --> 00:27:13,250
Hurry up. We're gonna miss the bus.

309
00:27:14,410 --> 00:27:17,050
No matter what I say, you're not
gonna break up with her, are you?

310
00:27:24,022 --> 00:27:26,000
If you're really set on leaving,

311
00:27:31,630 --> 00:27:33,160
I'll let you take the exam in Bangkok.

312
00:27:35,206 --> 00:27:37,480
And if you get in on your own,

313
00:27:39,376 --> 00:27:40,720
I'll support you

314
00:27:41,771 --> 00:27:42,960
and let you study there.

315
00:27:44,507 --> 00:27:45,508
You mean it?

316
00:27:45,638 --> 00:27:46,639
Yeah.

317
00:27:48,240 --> 00:27:50,900
But I'll never approve of
you being with that girl.

318
00:27:53,011 --> 00:27:56,080
When Mom died, Dad told me

319
00:27:58,019 --> 00:28:00,512
we don't get to choose
who we fall in love with.

320
00:28:02,614 --> 00:28:03,615
But we do get to choose

321
00:28:05,462 --> 00:28:07,902
what we're willing to give up
for what we want to hold on to.

322
00:28:09,931 --> 00:28:11,480
I didn't get it back then.

323
00:28:13,958 --> 00:28:14,959
Now I do.

324
00:28:25,651 --> 00:28:27,763
And stop thinking I'm so mean.

325
00:28:28,920 --> 00:28:31,000
I love you more than
anyone in this family, dumbass.

326
00:28:45,599 --> 00:28:47,552
[Applicant Details for
Srisilapasat University]

327
00:28:47,798 --> 00:28:50,640
What's this? Aren't we
going to the same university?

328
00:28:51,622 --> 00:28:52,623
We are.

329
00:28:53,307 --> 00:28:54,308
Look.

330
00:28:54,608 --> 00:28:57,000
I applied to Srisilapasat
too—the one you wanna go to.

331
00:28:57,910 --> 00:28:59,500
When did you apply?

332
00:29:02,062 --> 00:29:04,600
I don't want you giving
up on your dream for me.

333
00:29:05,459 --> 00:29:06,899
I'll work hard and get in on my own.

334
00:29:07,582 --> 00:29:09,854
And I'll figure out what I
wanna do with my life too.

335
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:13,001
We'll go together.

336
00:29:43,107 --> 00:29:44,712
Hey, you hungry?

337
00:29:46,108 --> 00:29:47,109
A little.

338
00:29:47,774 --> 00:29:48,775
I knew it.

339
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:59,050
You know me too well.

340
00:30:15,600 --> 00:30:16,800
This is so good.

341
00:30:26,646 --> 00:30:28,064
Wanna pray for some luck first?

342
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:31,401
Wait, aren't you Christian?

343
00:30:32,230 --> 00:30:35,900
Yeah, but it can't hurt.

344
00:30:36,680 --> 00:30:37,681
You never know.

345
00:30:38,238 --> 00:30:40,510
I'll take all the help I can get right now.

346
00:30:41,196 --> 00:30:43,720
I'm sure Buddha won't mind, right?

347
00:30:45,075 --> 00:30:46,996
Sure, why not?

348
00:30:59,507 --> 00:31:00,508
- Let's go.
- Go.

349
00:31:03,723 --> 00:31:04,724
Let me fix your shoes.

350
00:31:05,062 --> 00:31:06,063
What?

351
00:31:12,582 --> 00:31:14,200
Let's just do our best.

352
00:31:16,075 --> 00:31:17,076
Let's go.

353
00:31:25,500 --> 00:31:27,860
[Srisilapasat University Direct
Admission Exam Exam Room 1]

354
00:32:28,430 --> 00:32:29,431
How'd it go?

355
00:32:30,152 --> 00:32:31,153
I'm just glad it's over.

356
00:32:31,600 --> 00:32:34,040
I hope I get in. I really don't
wanna take another exam.

357
00:32:34,691 --> 00:32:36,692
You did great. You've got this.

358
00:32:38,142 --> 00:32:39,143
Come on.

359
00:32:44,611 --> 00:32:47,400
Our bus isn't until this evening.

360
00:32:47,993 --> 00:32:50,160
Wanna grab something
to eat before we head back?

361
00:32:51,120 --> 00:32:53,740
I was gonna ask you the same thing.

362
00:32:56,126 --> 00:32:58,280
Wherever you go, I'm going too.

363
00:32:58,900 --> 00:32:59,901
Let's stick together.

364
00:33:01,944 --> 00:33:03,918
- You promise?
- Yeah.

365
00:33:04,062 --> 00:33:05,800
- Are you sure?
- I'm sure.

366
00:33:06,808 --> 00:33:09,009
You can't leave me, okay?

367
00:33:12,995 --> 00:33:13,996
Okay, I promise.

368
00:33:17,272 --> 00:33:18,600
Hey!

369
00:33:19,191 --> 00:33:20,192
I promise.

370
00:35:18,544 --> 00:35:20,720
I wish we could stay here forever.

371
00:35:22,400 --> 00:35:25,120
Soon, we really will.

372
00:35:25,701 --> 00:35:26,702
We'll be here together.

373
00:35:32,216 --> 00:35:34,800
♪ A gentle breeze blows by ♪

374
00:35:34,920 --> 00:35:37,360
♪ And tears begin to fall ♪

375
00:35:37,523 --> 00:35:39,960
♪ Only the scent of love remains ♪

376
00:35:40,205 --> 00:35:42,680
♪ Lingering in my loneliness ♪

377
00:35:42,803 --> 00:35:47,880
♪ Our love has yet to fade,
still etched upon my heart ♪

378
00:35:48,152 --> 00:35:51,320
♪ Its sweet fragrance
still haunts my dreams ♪

379
00:35:51,629 --> 00:35:56,040
♪ All that remains is a
scent that never fades ♪

380
00:35:56,960 --> 00:36:01,440
♪ Still as sweet as it was
when the breeze blows by ♪

381
00:36:02,280 --> 00:36:06,481
♪ Leaving only memories
that can never return ♪

382
00:36:08,300 --> 00:36:10,101
Every time I'm with you, Blue,

383
00:36:10,501 --> 00:36:11,798
my heart never stops racing.

384
00:36:12,032 --> 00:36:14,320
I never want

385
00:36:16,320 --> 00:36:18,400
any of our days together

386
00:36:18,508 --> 00:36:19,640
to end.

387
00:36:19,732 --> 00:36:21,800
♪ Your sweetness is too much to resist ♪

388
00:36:22,016 --> 00:36:24,520
♪ My heart flutters every time ♪

389
00:36:26,668 --> 00:36:29,569
I don't know

390
00:36:30,310 --> 00:36:31,990
if this is what liking someone feels like.

391
00:36:32,960 --> 00:36:34,400
But I think I like you, Blue.

392
00:36:34,460 --> 00:36:38,200
♪ All that remains is a
scent that never fades ♪

393
00:36:39,161 --> 00:36:43,680
♪ Still as sweet as it was
when the breeze blows by ♪

394
00:36:44,480 --> 00:36:48,760
♪ Leaving only memories
that can never return ♪

395
00:36:49,651 --> 00:36:52,252
♪ I keep you hidden in my heart ♪

396
00:37:05,680 --> 00:37:09,680
♪ Leaving only a past
that can never return ♪

397
00:37:10,840 --> 00:37:13,341
♪ I keep you hidden in my heart ♪

398
00:37:28,179 --> 00:37:29,400
Ever done it before?

399
00:37:40,700 --> 00:37:41,701
No, but I want to.

400
00:39:29,331 --> 00:39:30,332
Are we gonna make it?

401
00:39:30,819 --> 00:39:31,880
There! Over there!

402
00:39:33,656 --> 00:39:34,657
Hey!

403
00:39:38,294 --> 00:39:39,800
Oh, shit. We're really screwed now.

404
00:39:41,046 --> 00:39:42,806
- Hey!
- Hey!

405
00:39:43,739 --> 00:39:46,300
Sorry, we're closed. No more buses tonight.

406
00:39:47,331 --> 00:39:48,332
What do we do?

407
00:39:48,440 --> 00:39:51,841
But if you hurry, there's
one last van out back.

408
00:39:52,360 --> 00:39:54,250
- That one?
- Yeah, just go.

409
00:39:54,771 --> 00:39:56,440
- Hurry up.
- Thank you.

410
00:40:10,974 --> 00:40:12,700
How'd it go, Dad? Everything work out?

411
00:40:14,300 --> 00:40:15,816
Couldn't have gone better.

412
00:40:16,622 --> 00:40:18,182
Not only did I get the money we needed,

413
00:40:18,374 --> 00:40:20,320
they're gonna invest with us too.

414
00:40:20,656 --> 00:40:22,200
We're celebrating tonight!

415
00:40:23,360 --> 00:40:24,361
Big!

416
00:40:25,261 --> 00:40:27,720
Order a big pot of sukiyaki for everyone.

417
00:40:28,762 --> 00:40:29,763
Sure, Dad.

418
00:40:40,763 --> 00:40:41,764
Where's Tokyo?

419
00:40:50,896 --> 00:40:52,000
No idea, Dad.

420
00:40:52,683 --> 00:40:54,076
I haven't seen her since this morning.

421
00:40:54,100 --> 00:40:55,640
I saw Miss Tokyo this morning, sir.

422
00:40:58,000 --> 00:40:59,001
What the hell?

423
00:40:59,904 --> 00:41:01,464
If you've got something to say, say it.

424
00:41:01,819 --> 00:41:02,960
Cat got your tongue?

425
00:41:04,820 --> 00:41:07,280
Or do I have to make you talk at gunpoint?

426
00:41:08,240 --> 00:41:11,480
I saw Tokyo leave the house
in her school uniform before dawn, Boss.

427
00:41:12,300 --> 00:41:13,520
That's all I know.

428
00:41:16,550 --> 00:41:19,600
Don't worry, Dad.
I'll have the cops search the whole town.

429
00:41:22,118 --> 00:41:23,700
Get our guys out looking too.

430
00:41:24,800 --> 00:41:25,840
Find her.

431
00:41:37,323 --> 00:41:38,324
Go!

432
00:41:41,800 --> 00:41:42,801
Shit.

433
00:41:43,342 --> 00:41:44,443
We're so screwed.

434
00:41:50,558 --> 00:41:51,559
God...

435
00:41:51,760 --> 00:41:53,761
[Get back here now. Dad knows.]

436
00:41:54,708 --> 00:41:56,160
Call me if you hear anything.

437
00:42:00,368 --> 00:42:02,700
Pakkad said Blue still hasn't
gone back to the dorm.

438
00:42:03,490 --> 00:42:04,640
And it's already this late.

439
00:42:21,864 --> 00:42:23,400
- Yi!
- Mom!

440
00:42:27,499 --> 00:42:28,500
Dad!

441
00:42:33,256 --> 00:42:34,257
Blue!

442
00:43:08,262 --> 00:43:09,379
[Next Episode]
From now on,

443
00:43:09,403 --> 00:43:12,120
you're not to contact anyone whatsoever.

444
00:43:12,352 --> 00:43:13,653
Forget about Tokyo.

445
00:43:13,718 --> 00:43:16,120
From now on, you're moving back home.

446
00:43:16,750 --> 00:43:19,363
I think you and your girlfriend
should leave this town as soon as possible.

447
00:43:19,387 --> 00:43:22,240
I have a feeling our family
and theirs will clash sooner or later.

448
00:43:22,588 --> 00:43:23,902
If we want to put an end to all this,

449
00:43:23,926 --> 00:43:25,827
we may have to work together to find out

450
00:43:26,240 --> 00:43:27,480
how it all began

451
00:43:28,000 --> 00:43:29,401
17 years ago...

452
00:43:30,331 --> 00:43:32,000
what happened to Mom?
